[11.8, "o", "\r\n"]
[12.1, "o", "The evidence on intermittent fasting and insulin sensitivity is extensive but mixed, with\r\n"]
[12.4, "o", "important caveats about age, population, and study quality.\r\n"]
[12.7, "o", "\r\n"]
[13.0, "o", "A meta-analysis of 8 RCTs (573 participants) found that fasting significantly decreased HOMA-IR in\r\n"]
[13.3, "o", "adults (WMD = -0.60; 95% CI: -0.91, -0.28; P < 0.001) [2].\r\n"]
[13.6, "o", "\r\n"]
[13.9, "o", "On HbA1c, however, the evidence conflicts. One meta-analysis found a significant HbA1c decrease\r\n"]
[14.2, "o", "[2], but another found that intermittent fasting diets did not significantly change HbA1c, with a\r\n"]
[14.5, "o", "mean reduction of 0.08% (95% CI: -0.25 to -0.10) [3]. These two findings are in direct conflict\r\n"]
[14.8, "o", "and both must be reported.\r\n"]
[15.4, "o", "\r\n"]
[15.8, "o", "                              [\u2026  five sections and 5 sources omitted  \u2026]\r\n"]
[16.7, "o", "\r\n"]
[17.0, "o", "## Sources\r\n"]
[17.4, "o", "\r\n"]
[17.7, "o", "[2] https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12363089\r\n"]
[18.0, "o", "    > and HOMA-IR (WMD= -0.60; 95% CI: -0.91, -0.28; P < 0.001) in adults.\r\n"]
[18.3, "o", "    > The GRADE quality of evidence for the effect of fasting on HOMA-IR was high.\r\n"]
[18.8, "o", "\r\n"]
[19.1, "o", "[3] https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8970877\r\n"]
[19.4, "o", "    > HOMA-IR decreased by 0.31 on an average (95% CIs: \u22120.44; \u22120.19).\r\n"]
